  s0: No owner row, the gateway serves (no node set)
  s1: No owner row, the gateway serves (no node set, the hub's file says otherwise, 1 file edit so far)
  s2: No owner row, the gateway serves (set to the designated node, 1 file edit so far)
  s3: No owner row, the gateway serves (set to the designated node, 1 file edit so far), an input waits at the gateway
  s4: No owner row, the gateway serves (set to the designated node, 1 file edit so far), turn runs on the gateway [an input ran on the wrong node]
  s5: No owner row, the gateway serves (set to the designated node, 1 file edit so far), idle session on the gateway [an input ran on the wrong node]
  s6: No owner row, the gateway serves (set to the designated node, 1 file edit so far), an input waits at the gateway, idle session on the gateway [an input ran on the wrong node]
  [*] --> s0
  s0 --> s1: an operator edits one node's config file
  s1 --> s2: the hub copies its setting to the database
  s2 --> s3: you send a message
  s3 --> s4: the gateway starts the turn itself
  s4 --> s5: the answer reaches Discord
  s5 --> s6: you send a message
  s6 --> s4: the gateway starts the turn itself
